// 2026-11-21 (landing 177d2e, row 8: DEF-730, form P730c = P730b's delta with N730; rulings l.22291, l.23320, l.23532, l.23643). DEF-290'S
// SELF-WIRING EXEMPTION ADMITTED BY THE HOLDER'S ROOT, NOT BY THE STORAGE WRITTEN: a store whose target reaches the holder through a pointer
// (`(<-(h.a)).p = ...`, `h.a.p = ...`) is self-wiring now only when the address stored is taken through that same pointer place (`@((<-(h.a)).k)`),
// or the pointer value stored is read through it, a slice on either path standing as the base before any pointer; anything else falls to the
// BORROW-002 refusal, as its by-name spelling does. PRICES OFF PARITY, DEF-741 (LOW, fails closed, made by this row; l.23643 ruled item 2): N730
// takes a slice base before any pointer as the self-wiring store's base. So when the store's target crosses a range through a pointer local or a
// holder field, a right store is refused (BORROW-002), while its by-name spelling is accepted. Way out: drop the range, or spell the store by name;
// BORROW-002's text names neither. Its three faces from AFA's cells, one case each below, each refused here (BORROW-002) and run right on main and
// on row 7 (AFA, l.23643; W2E2's runs); its by-name twin `self_wire_def741_wayout_afa_n_inl_bn_ok.npk` and its way out
// `self_wire_def741_wayout_afa_n_inl_wo_ok.npk` run 67 on main and here. The cases are AFA's cells with each declared name suffixed by the cell's,
// in the form of main's prices files.
